HiGHS 1.15.1's MODULE.bazel without rules_cuda and zlib.

The companion highs_build.patch says why: no CUDA anywhere (rules_cuda's
toolkit extension probes the host for a CUDA install at fetch time), and no
zlib, which nothing in the library calls. This hunk lives in a patch of its own
because Bazel 9 applies every hunk of a patch that touches MODULE.bazel to
MODULE.bazel ("CONTENT_DOES_NOT_MATCH_TARGET" on the BUILD.bazel hunks
otherwise). It takes effect only because Cadpole is the root module.

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -8,17 +8,3 @@ module(
 bazel_dep(name = "bazel_skylib", version = "1.9.0")
 bazel_dep(name = "platforms", version = "1.1.0")
 bazel_dep(name = "rules_cc", version = "0.2.20")
-bazel_dep(name = "zlib", version = "1.3.2")
-bazel_dep(name = "rules_cuda", version = "0.3.0")
-
-# Load the extension
-cuda = use_extension("@rules_cuda//cuda:extensions.bzl", "toolchain")
-cuda.toolkit(
-    name = "cuda",
-)
-
-# Use 'cuda' as the repository name
-# use_repo(cuda, "cuda")
-
-# Alias local_cuda
-use_repo(cuda, local_cuda = "cuda")
